Accepted new evidence:

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"(CPC Congress) CPC expounds on main objectives, tasks for next 5 years","publisher":"Xinhua","publication_date":"2022-10-16","url":"https://english.news.cn/20221016/8ecf5c8af8be476796ca1fbf556754a4/c.html","claim":"The 20th CPC Congress set national security consolidation and PLA centenary goals for 2027 as five-year objectives under Xi Jinping's report.","locator":"lines 14-29","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous official congress summary with explicit target-year objectives.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period evidence of leadership priorities and institutional direction.","ruler_attribution":"Party-state priorities under Xi Jinping's leadership.","contrary_evidence":["This is broad strategy rather than nuclear command evidence.","It does not show whether the goals improved or worsened nuclear risk."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.7","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"(CPC Congress) Full text of resolution on 19th CPC Central Committee report","publisher":"Xinhua","publication_date":"2022-10-22","url":"https://english.news.cn/20221022/74ad92bf38c444a2a7397b1f579a4bcc/c.html","claim":"The congress approved Xi Jinping's report and said Xi's core position and guiding thought must be decisively upheld across the Party.","locator":"lines 17-29","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official closing-session resolution with explicit institutional language about Xi's core status.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period evidence of political authority and constraint structure.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributes authority to Xi as Party core leader.","contrary_evidence":["This confirms authority, not responsible nuclear conduct.","It is self-affirming party text and not an independent monitor."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China's defense policy defense-oriented, peace-oriented","publisher":"english.www.gov.cn","publication_date":"2019-07-24","url":"https://english.www.gov.cn/policies/policywatch/201907/24/content_WS5d384696c6d08408f5022800.html","claim":"The defense white paper framed China's military policy as defense-oriented and peace-oriented and said China does not seek hegemony, expansion, or spheres of influence.","locator":"lines 45-49 and 58-70","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official state-policy summary with explicit baseline claims about defense posture and anti-hegemony language.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited baseline for Xi's 2022 posture; not target-year conduct itself.","ruler_attribution":"Inherited PRC defense posture under Xi-era leadership.","contrary_evidence":["This is declaratory policy, not implementation.","It does not establish how 2022 command decisions were actually made."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.3","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Chinese Delegation Attends the 10th Review Conference of the Parties to the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-08-05","url":"https://www.mfa.gov.cn/eng/wjb/zzjg_663340/jks_665232/jkxw_665234/202208/t20220805_10735079.html","claim":"China told the NPT Review Conference that it follows a self-defense nuclear strategy, maintains no-first-use, and keeps its nuclear capability at the minimum level required for national security.","locator":"lines 69-69","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary 2022 delegation statement with clear declaratory policy language and direct date fit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period arms-control and doctrine evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Official PRC position under Xi Jinping's leadership.","contrary_evidence":["Official doctrine is not proof of actual restraint.","Independent sources report simultaneous expansion and modernization."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Statement by H.E. Amb. LI Song on Nuclear Disarmament at the Tenth NPT Review Conference","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-08-05","url":"https://www.mfa.gov.cn/eng/wjb/zzjg_663340/jks_665232/kjfywj_665252/202406/t20240606_11405407.html","claim":"China called for CTBT entry into force, support for FMCT negotiations, P5 strategic-risk-reduction work, and stronger anti-arms-race language.","locator":"lines 89-93","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary 2022 NPT statement with specific arms-control positions and risk-reduction language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period arms-control evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Official Chinese diplomatic position under Xi-era policy.","contrary_evidence":["These are pledges and preferences, not proof of implementation.","China still had not ratified the CTBT."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Statement by H.E. Amb. LI Song on Nuclear Non-Proliferation at the Tenth NPT Review Conference","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-08-08","url":"https://www.mfa.gov.cn/eng/wjb/zzjg_663340/jks_665252/kjfywj_665252/202406/t20240606_11405408.html","claim":"China argued that AUKUS nuclear-submarine cooperation and nuclear sharing are proliferation risks and urged the major powers to handle Korea and Iran through political and diplomatic means.","locator":"lines 73-91","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary 2022 delegation statement with concrete proliferation and de-escalation positions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period evidence on proliferation and de-escalation.","ruler_attribution":"Official Chinese policy under Xi Jinping's leadership.","contrary_evidence":["It is a position paper, not implementation evidence.","China's own modernization program continued in parallel."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.6","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"10. World nuclear forces","publisher":"Stockholm International Peace Research Institute","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://www.sipri.org/yearbook/2022/10","claim":"SIPRI said China was in significant nuclear modernization and expansion, including over 300 new missile silos, while releasing little information about force numbers and future development plans.","locator":"lines 92-101","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent technical yearbook from a leading open-source nuclear research institute.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 posture assessment and inherited-baseline context.","ruler_attribution":"Xi-era strategic posture and modernization trajectory.","contrary_evidence":["China's official line remains minimum deterrence and NFU.","SIPRI does not prove launch authority or crisis intent."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China Is Building A Second Nuclear Missile Silo Field","publisher":"Federation of American Scientists","publication_date":"2021-07-26","url":"https://fas.org/publication/china-is-building-a-second-nuclear-missile-silo-field/","claim":"FAS said the Hami and Yumen silo construction was the most significant expansion of the Chinese nuclear arsenal ever and that roughly 250 silos were under construction.","locator":"lines 63-100","source_type":"ngo","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent satellite-based technical analysis with specific imagery-derived findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 inherited baseline that directly conditions the 2022 posture.","ruler_attribution":"Inherited strategic posture under Xi-era leadership.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not prove warhead loading or alert status.","China still publicly described the force as minimum and defensive."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Engaging China on Strategic Stability and Mutual Vulnerability","publisher":"Carnegie Endowment for International Peace","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://carnegieendowment.org/research/2022/10/engaging-china-on-strategic-stability-and-mutual-vulnerability?lang=en","claim":"Perkovich argued that China and the United States are mutually vulnerable to nuclear destruction and that the growing Chinese force and strategic dialogue problem require explicit strategic-stability engagement.","locator":"lines 24-37 and 65-85","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"High-quality policy scholarship that ties 2022 Chinese buildup to strategic-stability and dialogue concerns.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 strategic context.","ruler_attribution":"Xi-era strategic environment and decision context.","contrary_evidence":["This is analysis, not primary evidence of Xi's choices.","It is more diagnostic than adjudicative."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China's Xi clinches third term, packs leadership with loyalists","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-23","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/chinas-xi-clinches-third-term-packs-leadership-with-loyalists-2919033","claim":"Reuters reported that Xi won a precedent-breaking third term, the new Standing Committee was stacked with loyalists, and there was no clear successor in sight.","locator":"lines 430-460","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on elite composition and succession constraints.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period evidence of ruler authority and institutional insulation.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributes dominance to Xi and his chosen cadre.","contrary_evidence":["This does not prove nuclear restraint or recklessness.","It is political reporting, not command-and-control evidence."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Chinese ex-President Hu Jintao escorted out of party congress","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-22","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/chinese-expresident-hu-jintao-escorted-out-of-party-congress-2918972","claim":"Reuters reported that Hu Jintao was unexpectedly escorted out of the congress closing session, the scene was censored from state coverage, and the closing amendments cemented Xi's core status.","locator":"lines 431-455","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters witness reporting of a major elite-management event with official censoring evidence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 elite-control and institutional-power evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Occurs in Xi's presence and within Xi-consolidated party authority.","contrary_evidence":["The official explanation said Hu was unwell.","The incident does not by itself show nuclear decision quality."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China halts high-level military dialogue with U.S., suspends other cooperation","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-08-05","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/beijing-halts-highlevel-military-dialogue-with-us-suspends-other-cooperation-2864888","claim":"After Pelosi's Taiwan visit, China suspended dialogue between senior-level military commanders and cancelled a maritime military security meeting, worsening crisis-management channels.","locator":"lines 418-424","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on a concrete escalation decision with direct crisis-communication implications.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 crisis-management evidence.","ruler_attribution":"State action under Xi's leadership.","contrary_evidence":["Beijing framed the move as retaliation for Pelosi's visit.","The article does not show nuclear-use intent."],"lenses":["1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)","publisher":"CTBTO","publication_date":"undated","url":"https://www.ctbto.org/resources/information-materials/frequently-asked-questions","claim":"CTBTO states that China signed the CTBT on 24 September 1996 but has not yet ratified it.","locator":"lines 377-381","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IGO treaty-status FAQ with explicit ratification status and stable legal context.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Stable treaty-status background applicable in 2022 and later.","ruler_attribution":"State-level treaty posture under Xi-era policy.","contrary_evidence":["China separately says it supports CTBT entry into force and a test moratorium.","Non-ratification alone does not prove readiness to test."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"How is China Modernizing its Nuclear Forces?","publisher":"CSIS ChinaPower Project","publication_date":"undated","url":"https://chinapower.csis.org/china-nuclear-weapons/","claim":"The page says the 2022 DoD report assessed that the PLA was implementing a launch-on-warning posture and that China likely had at least three early-warning satellites in orbit by 2022.","locator":"lines 97-102","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent policy synthesis that directly interprets the 2022 posture using official and open-source inputs.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Explicitly tied to 2022 posture.","ruler_attribution":"Xi-era modernization and posture trajectory.","contrary_evidence":["This is an analytical synthesis, not a Chinese admission.","A launch-on-warning assessment is not the same as proof of operational intent."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Position Paper of the People's Republic of China on Strengthening Ethical Governance of Artificial Intelligence (AI)","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-11-17","url":"https://www.mfa.gov.cn/mfa_eng/zy/wjzc/202405/t20240531_11367525.html","claim":"China said AI can create safety and security risks and called for ethics review, regulation, human control, transparency, and precaution across AI development and use.","locator":"body text sections I-4","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary 2022 policy paper with detailed AI governance prescriptions and explicit risk language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 dual-use and catastrophic-risk governance evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Official PRC governance position under Xi-era leadership.","contrary_evidence":["This is policy language, not implementation evidence.","It is about governance norms rather than nuclear command."],"lenses":["1B.9","1B.7","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Report on Military and Security Developments Involving the People's Republic of China","publisher":"U.S. Department of Defense","publication_date":"2022-11-29","url":"https://www.defense.gov/News/Releases/Release/Article/3230516/2022-report-on-military-and-security-developments-involving-the-peoples-republi/","claim":"The Department of Defense released its 2022 China military report as an authoritative assessment of PRC military and security strategy.","locator":"lines 192-211","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous U.S. government release announcing an authoritative annual assessment.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 institutional context for all later nuclear-force claims.","ruler_attribution":"Assessment of Xi-led PRC strategy rather than personal attribution.","contrary_evidence":["This release page is procedural rather than substantive.","The detailed findings are in the report, not the announcement page."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.10"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidates found: about 55 plausible documents across official Chinese, treaty, independent technical, scholarship, and Reuters families.
- Documents opened: 30+ promising documents were opened when accessible.
- Duplicate families discarded: about 18, mostly Reuters mirrors, repeated official reposts, and overlapping treaty/arms-control pages.
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items discarded: about 9.
- Inaccessible or JS-gated items discarded: about 4.
- Accepted distinct URLs: 16.
- Retained domains: 10.

Material gaps and next-best directions:
- I still do not have a direct 2022 Chinese military, CMC, or Rocket Force document showing how Xi personally handled nuclear command, custody, or launch authority.
- The best missing area for 1B.3 is Chinese command-and-control detail: early-warning integration, Rocket Force readiness, custody discipline, and any explicit launch-posture change in 2022.
- The best missing area for 1B.8 is more direct crisis-channel evidence around Taiwan, especially contemporaneous U.S., Japanese, or UN diplomatic records on military-to-military deconfliction.
- The best missing area for 1B.9 is implementation-level dual-use governance, especially Chinese cyber, space, AI, or bio-security enforcement records, not just policy statements.
- The strongest next query family is Chinese-language PLA/CMC/Rocket Force material plus one more independent technical source on launch-on-warning and early-warning architecture.
